@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080

### Platform stats
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/stats

### The competency catalog every listing and profile is built from
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/competencies

### Open listings, newest first (sorted by match score once you are signed in)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/listings

### Listings that need a specific area
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/listings?competency=graphics

### People directory with filters
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users?competency=gamedev&openOnly=true

### Log in as the demo student (all demo accounts use the password demo1234)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "demo@example.com",
  "password": "demo1234"
}

###
@token = {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Current user
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One listing, including your own match score and breakdown
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/listings/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Everyone who applied or was invited to your listing, best match first
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/listings/1/applications
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### People worth inviting to your own open listings
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/suggestions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Your requests inbox, both directions
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/applications
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Write the suitability report for an applicant (owner only).
### Uses the configured model, or the built-in rule-based writer when there is no API key.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/applications/1/review
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Accept a request. Contact details are revealed to both sides afterwards.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/applications/1/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Import your public repositories from GitHub
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me/github
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Post a listing
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/listings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Study timer that syncs with the course schedule",
  "summary": "The API is done. I need someone to design and build the interface.",
  "description": "ASP.NET Core back end with accounts and a schedule importer. There is no front end at all yet.",
  "needs": [
    { "slug": "frontend", "isPrimary": true },
    { "slug": "uiux", "isPrimary": false }
  ],
  "stack": ["React", "TypeScript", "ASP.NET Core"],
  "projectUrl": "",
  "teamSize": 1,
  "hoursPerWeek": 8,
  "timeline": "6 weeks"
}

### Apply to someone else's listing
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/listings/2/apply
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "I have built the back end of a habit tracker before and this is the part I enjoy. I have 10 hours a week."
}

### Invite someone to one of your listings. They decide.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/listings/1/invite
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 13,
  "message": "Your pixel art is exactly the style I had in mind for the jam. Would you like to join?"
}

### Mark a listing as completed (owner only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/listings/1/complete
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "note": "We built the game prototype, finished 5 levels, and submitted to the game jam!"
}

### Cancel a listing (owner only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/listings/1/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "note": "The project scope was too large and team members had conflicting schedules."
}

### Cancel an active collaboration (owner or accepted applicant)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/applications/1/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Unable to dedicate required hours due to exams."
}
